# NFL photo jersey backs (always)

**One silhouette.** Philadelphia Eagles elite cut (V-neck, short sleeves with cuff bands, upper-back nameplate, mesh fabric). Solid `#000` (LED energy). No hanger on photo backs.

**Scale lock:** PNG jersey must fill the frame — **never shrink** for collar/helmet. CSS uses **width-based** `background-size: 88% auto`. Uniform shift: `--nfl-photo-stack-y` (default `4%`) moves jersey PNG + patron overlays together via `calc()` on `background-position` and overlay `top`. Font caps unchanged (~11.5vh name, ~48vh number).

**Helmet:** Optional side mascot/helmet in PNG only after jersey stack is locked; must not touch the right sleeve.

**Wordmark:** baked into the PNG only (club on nameplate). Upright athletic block caps. CSS hides `.soccer-jersey-team` on photo kits.

**Patron name (CSS):** base `top` ~18% + `var(--nfl-photo-stack-y)`; cap ~11.5vh.

**Number (CSS):** base `top` ~40% + shift; cap ~48vh.

**Dual shoutout layout (`nfl-jersey` / `nflDualLayout`):**
- **96×48:** jersey left-justified; white text shoutout on the right (4 lines × 16 = 64 graphemes, emoji OK); FloqR card bottom; kit-color edge glow.
- **64×48 / 64×32:** rotate jersey phase ↔ text phase (frame 2 = **solid black** + white shoutout; jersey fully hidden). FloqR card on both. **64×32:** 3 lines × 16 = 48 graphemes.
- FloqR card Instagram/handle is **opt-in** and **independent** of jersey name (`includeAttribution` + `attributionChoice` vs `soccerNameSource` / `jerseyPatronName`). Checkout must use `nflJersey` text caps (not soccer 8–12).

